<title>MALAYSIA: Maybank sees 1.87 bln ringgit gain.</title>
<headline>Maybank sees 1.87 bln ringgit gain.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian banking giant Malayan Banking Bhd (Maybank) said the sale of subsidiary Kwong Yik Bank would result in an extraordinary gain of about 1.87 billion ringgit for the year ending June 30 1997.</p>
<p>On Tuesday Maybank announced it would sell its 75-percent owned unit to Rashid Hussain Bhd at 8.80 ringgit ($3.50) per share in the biggest bank merger in Malaysian corporate history.  </p>
<p>Maybank managing director Amir Sham Aziz told reporters at a news conference that Maybank's shares, which were suspended on October 21, would now be requoted on the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange on Monday, December 2.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom, +65 870 3174</p>
</text>
